2026-09-27T09:57:29.3545847Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3546214Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3546522Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3547415Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3548521Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3548634Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3548871Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3549198Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3549497Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3549592Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3549815Z ================
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3549968Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3550135Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3550544Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3550777Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3550912Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3551237Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3551415Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3551573Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3552046Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3552455Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3553191Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3553772Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3613936Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3614644Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3615275Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3615590Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3615989Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:57:29.3616485Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4983492Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4983725Z ========
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4983834Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4984858Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4985908Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4986121Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4986482Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4987227Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4987829Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4988264Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4988591Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4988927Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4989014Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4989210Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4989317Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4990087Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4990885Z 
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4991360Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4992008Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:57:29.4992173Z 
